 "result_text": "I fixed the `IndexError` when `icr_custom_value` is 0. I haven't run any tests or the code itself.\n\n- **Cause:** `icr_lux_display` in `src/uiprotect/data/devices.py` looks up `LUX_MAPPING_VALUES[10 - icr_custom_value]`. That list has 10 entries (indices 0\u20139), so a value of 0 asks for index 10.\n- **Fix:** `icr_lux_display` now returns `0` when `icr_custom_value` is 0, matching the \"under 1 lux\" setting.\n- **Related change:** I also lowered the minimum of `ICRLuxValue` in `src/uiprotect/data/types.py` from 1 to 0. This lets `set_icr_custom_lux(0)` pass validation, and it already maps to an `icr_custom_value` of 0. This one is my addition beyond the crash itself, so say if you'd rather keep the old minimum.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
